"""DoodlebookOS Material You icon theme — generated, not filtered.

Like Android 13+ "themed icons": every installed application gets a monochrome glyph (brand logo
from Simple Icons, else a Material Symbol, else its initial) on a tonal circle; folders and file
types are drawn as Material 3 shapes. All colours come from the wallpaper palette given by
doodlebookos-materialyou, which calls this on every wallpaper change.

  doodlebookos-m3icons build OUT --name NAME --inherits BASE --palette JSON
  doodlebookos-m3icons signature      # changes when the set of application icons changes
  doodlebookos-m3icons apps           # which glyph each application gets

Glyphs: ~/.local/share/doodlebookos/m3icons (Material Symbols Apache-2.0, Simple Icons CC0, letters
from Google Sans Flex). Per-app overrides: ~/.config/doodlebookos/m3icons.map, lines "icon-or-desktop-id = ms:name | si:slug | letter:X".
"""
